Horus v@PROJECT_VERSION@ adds persistent case analysis without changing the direct workflow: dropping a file onto the executable or running `horus.exe sample.exe` still analyzes it immediately.

Highlights:

- Persistent Case Mode for up to 5,000 samples, with incremental refresh, verify, rebuild, prune, portable state, and offline HTML/CSV/JSON reports.
- Exact duplicate groups for every file and explainable PE similarity clusters based on TLSH, imphash, Rich hash, and section layout.
- Content-based direct analysis for files with any extension, including drag-and-drop and paths with spaces.
- Explicit `UNKNOWN` and `analysis_status` output when evidence is unavailable, plus documented exit code 3 for incomplete results.
- Opt-in network enrichment with `--enrich`; only hashes and extracted indicators are sent, never file contents.
- Offline/cache-only Authenticode trust by default, with online revocation available through `--online-trust`.
- Hardened report embedding, strict JSON parsing, bounded HTTP responses, atomic state/export writes, and CSV formula protection.

The three binaries target Windows 10/11 x64. They are not Authenticode-signed; verify downloads with `SHA256SUMS.txt` and GitHub artifact attestations.
